=1.1`. `m027_turns_response_json` adds the column.\n- **`llm/logs.py`:**\n  - The new helpers are `_payload_replacements`, `condense_payload`, `resolve_payload` and `_model_json_replacements`, plus `TURN_TOOLS_SQL`.\n  - `LogStore.log` writes the condensed payload.\n  - `turn_response_json` and `_turn_tool_pairs` are new on `LogStore`.\n  - `llm logs` rows now carry the resolved payload through `_resolve_response_json`. A payload that no longer resolves gives `None` for that row instead of failing the listing.\n- **`llm/default_plugins/openai_models.py`:** both `Responses.execute` and `AsyncResponses.execute` now yield a refresh event after the final payload, via `_reasoning_refresh_events`. A streamed reasoning part therefore keeps one ciphertext, the one in the final payload.\n\nI also reworded the comment above `\"prompt_json\": None` in `_LogRowBuilder.build`, since it said the raw payload wasn't stored.", "ttft_ms": 6493, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 82902, "uuid": "97e41464-b038-4080-818f-98ae02ae4e44", "ttft_stream_ms": 6039, "time_to_request_ms": 53, "first_content_frame_ms": 6039, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
